  "body": "Follow-up of #4334 (U8 of #3663).\n\n## What happens\n\nThe footer of the tool editor in the tool library window shows **Duplicate**. The button is disabled. Its hover text gives the reason.\n\nNo command copies a tool together with its holder and its component stack. `AddTool` with the stored tool makes a copy without the holder (it applies the machine's default holder). That copy is different from the source tool, and the user does not see the difference.\n\n## Expected\n\n- Duplicate makes a new document tool from the open tool: the same geometry, cutting data, holder, stick-out and component stack, a free name and the next free tool number.\n- The copy is one undoable command, with its MCP tool (or a filed `MCP:` issue).\n- The window opens the copy in the editor.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A command test: the copy has the holder and the stack of the source; one undo removes it.\n- The UI test of the footer asserts that Duplicate is enabled and opens the copy.\n",
